#/-------------------[DOTENV_PUBLIC_KEY]--------------------/
#/            public-key encryption for .env files          /
#/       [how it works](https://dotenvx.com/encryption)     /
#/----------------------------------------------------------/
DOTENV_PUBLIC_KEY_LOCAL="020b1ca714a3dafe2597646bc5044d8357c1e38849ef80a7a6edcd28a2f071effd"

# .env.local
# Local Supabase stack (supabase start, project ivaecofevxactmmupvyp mirror).
# Loaded by `bun run dev:local` ahead of the encrypted .env — first file wins.
# Plain `bun run dev` ignores this file and still uses the hosted project.
#
# Committed *encrypted* by dotenvx, same as .env — decrypt with
# DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY_LOCAL from .env.keys, which is never committed. Every
# value here belongs to the LOCAL stack and grants nothing on the hosted
# project; `supabase start` regenerates the same pair from config.toml, so a
# teammate who cannot decrypt can just read them off its output.
#
# NAMING RULE (see .env.example): VITE_* is inlined into public JavaScript at
# build time. Never give the secret key a VITE_ prefix.
#
# URL NOTE: the API gateway is Kong, published on host port 54321. The
# `supabase_studio_ivaecofevxactmmupvyp.orb.local` hostname is the Studio
# dashboard container (host port 54323), not the API — and *.orb.local does
# not resolve on this machine (no /etc/resolver/orb.local). Studio UI:
# http://127.0.0.1:54323 — Mailpit (local inbox): http://127.0.0.1:54324

# ── Browser-exposed: the only vars app/lib/supabase.ts reads ──
